  "statement": "With k_sh = 1.4 kN / 0.025 mm = 56 kN/mm (js4) and the clamped-wall k_c 1.60e6 N/mm, a screw stiffness k_b 1.58e5 N/mm reproduces js4's +927 N at the GVLO soak frame (fit stays closed, residual fit contact 879 N): the joint stiffness for an axial mismatch is 1.44e5 N/mm with the fit closed and 41 kN/mm with it open, against the v2 stiff hand value k_bm 3.65e5 (k_b 4.73e5: A_s over the grip, E_steel in the tapped part); the VDI-form screw resilience gives k_b 2.35e5 (closed k_J 2.06e5, js4 frame +1322 N). The v2 hand rise at that frame was 2674 N because it put the ring growth (d_r 42.3 um) through the screw in series with a 21 kN/mm shell; with the fit closed the ring growth mainly unloads the fit contact."
